proper air and ventilation; 

g) the nature of the ground on which the proposed building is to be erected, whether 
natural like, rocky, gravelly, clayey, sandy etc., or made up ground. In the case of 
made up ground, the time when it was so made up and the materials used in 
making it up shall be indicated.  In case of sloping ground where the gradient 
exceeds 5% (1:20) block levels have to be furnished in the site plan; 

h) any physical features such as wells, drains, transmission lines, etc.; 

i) 
